Package: orangepi5b-va-driver
Version: @PACKAGE_VERSION@
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: Orange Pi 5B Builder <pencil.bsp@gmail.com>
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Depends: libva2 (>= @LIBVA_VERSION@)
Description: VA-API driver for the Orange Pi 5B video codecs
 Bridges libva to the V4L2 stateless codecs on RK3588S. H.264 and HEVC decode
 run on the mainline rkvdec driver; AV1 has a Hantro block of its own and the
 driver picks the device from the codec.
 .
 Chrome on Linux has no V4L2 decode path -- it is compiled behind
 BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS) -- so VA-API is the only way to reach these blocks from
 a desktop browser. GNOME Remote Desktop likewise encodes through VA-API.
 .
 Built against the libva of this release: a VA-API driver exports a
 version-stamped entry point, so one built for a different libva is never
 loaded and the client only reports that vaInitialize failed.
